   {
    "context": "It's what the church taught. But there are, of course, disputes, even going back to someone like Tertullian, who disputed this, that he supported it, and later he became a heretic. He joined the Motanists, the kind of these charismatic followers of the new prophecy in the third century, and he came to uh rebuke what he originally had taught about Peter because he believed authority should go with people who had particular charisms or or prophecies.",
